v 3
d srctag: modules to stamp variables with source lineage and search it
d
d srctag writes a variable's origin -- source, vintage, notes, and the
d structured fields agency, dataset, url, and category -- into its
d characteristics, the metadata slot that survives save and travels
d with the dataset through every later merge and append. It refuses to
d change an existing tag unless told replace, keeps a dataset-level
d manifest of every source in _dta[sources], and can sign the data
d with -datasignature- so stale provenance is caught instead of
d trusted. Companion command srcfind searches the tags: in memory or
d across a whole folder of .dta files (read header-only in a frame,
d so nothing in memory is disturbed), with contains, exact, wildcard,
d and case-sensitive matching, an untagged audit, inverted matches,
d results in r(varlist) and a macro of your choosing, and a
d machine-readable export of every tag as a dataset. srcfind tags and
d srcfind values browse the tagging vocabulary a file already uses.
d Pairs with datadictionary (SSC), which harvests the source tag into
d its codebook workbook.
d
d Requires: Stata 16.0 or newer.
d
d A test battery ships with the package as an ancillary file; retrieve
d it with -net get srctag- and run it with -do test_srctag.do-.
d
d Authors: Eric A. Booth
d          Elizabeth Teas
d Support: eric.a.booth@gmail.com
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260808
d
f srctag.ado
f srctag.sthlp
f srcfind.ado
f srcfind.sthlp
f test_srctag.do
